<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RebelAlliance_Suppress.xml                 Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-12
  ============================================================================

  THE GOAL  (NEXT_RELOAD item W6)
  ===============================
  Keep Outer Rim - Rebel Alliance ENABLED for its content — weapons, apparel,
  pawnkinds, backstories — while keeping the FACTION off the world map. The
  campaign is a Jawa scavenger clan; a galactic-civil-war belligerent holding
  settlements is not wanted, but the A280 on a scavenged rack is.

  So this is a suppression, NOT a removal. Success is a NEGATIVE observation:
  no Rebel Alliance settlement anywhere on the world map, AND
  OuterRim_A280Blaster still resolvable.

  WHY IT IS NEEDED  [VERIFIED 2026-08-12, from disk, game down]
  =============================================================
  Source of truth, read directly:

    .../workshop/content/294100/2919249903/1.6/Defs/FactionDefs/FactionDefs.xml

      <defName>OuterRim_RebelAlliance</defName>
      <settlementGenerationWeight>0.3</settlementGenerationWeight>
      <requiredCountAtGameStart>1</requiredCountAtGameStart>
      <canMakeRandomly>true</canMakeRandomly>
      <maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>9999</maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>

  requiredCountAtGameStart=1 is the one that matters. It does not merely make
  the faction likely, it makes it MANDATORY: RimWorld forces the count at world
  generation, and also tops up missing required factions when an existing save
  is loaded. Enabling this mod without suppression therefore plants the faction
  whether or not a new world is rolled. Weight 0.3 then keeps placing bases and
  canMakeRandomly=true lets more appear later.

  The parent, OuterRimDiverseFactionBase (Outer Rim Core, WS 2919227155,
  1.6/Defs/FactionDefs/Faction__Base.xml line 4), is Abstract and declares only
  maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation. Every field below is literally present in the
  child def, so all four ops are plain Replaces with nothing inherited behind
  them.

  WHY REPLACE THE NUMBERS AND NOT DELETE THE DEF
  ==============================================
  The def is referenced by name elsewhere in the same mod:

    2919249903/1.6/Defs/ScenarioDefs/Scenario_Rebel.xml:115
        <factionDef>OuterRim_RebelAlliance</factionDef>

  Deleting the FactionDef would turn that into a "Could not resolve
  cross-reference" on every launch — trading a world-map annoyance for a red
  error. Zeroing the generation fields leaves every reference intact.

  Nothing here touches a ThingDef. OuterRim_A280Blaster lives in
  1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Weapons/A280BlasterRifle.xml and is not faction-owned, so
  the weapon, its bullet and all Rebel gear remain fully resolvable. Pawnkinds
  are likewise untouched — Rebel troopers can still arrive as any other event
  spawns them, they simply have no territory.

  SCOPE — WHAT THIS DOES NOT DO
  =============================
  This is world-GENERATION suppression. It does not retroactively delete a
  Rebel Alliance faction from a save where one has already been generated. If
  the faction is already in the current world, it stays until a new world is
  rolled (or is removed by other means).

  maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation=0 also removes the faction from the world
  -creation faction picker, so it cannot be re-added by accident. That is
  deliberate; to opt back in, revert that one op rather than the whole file.

  SAFETY
  ======
  Every op is wrapped in PatchOperationConditional on the exact element, so if
  Rebel Alliance is not loaded, or an update renames/drops a field, the op is a
  silent no-op instead of a red error. test and inner xpath are identical here
  by design — this is a replace-if-present shape, not add-if-missing.

  VERIFY AFTER THE NEXT LOAD
  ==========================
    * NEGATIVE: no "Rebel Alliance" settlement on the world map. Check the
      faction list in the world view, not just the visible tiles.
    * POSITIVE: OuterRim_A280Blaster still resolves — spawn one via dev mode,
      and confirm no "Could not resolve cross-reference" naming it.
    * POSITIVE: no error naming OuterRim_RebelAlliance from Scenario_Rebel.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- The decisive one: stop the faction being forced into existence. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OuterRim_RebelAlliance"]/requiredCountAtGameStart</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OuterRim_RebelAlliance"]/requiredCountAtGameStart</xpath>
      <value>
        <requiredCountAtGameStart>0</requiredCountAtGameStart>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- No weight, so world gen never places a base for it. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OuterRim_RebelAlliance"]/settlementGenerationWeight</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OuterRim_RebelAlliance"]/settlementGenerationWeight</xpath>
      <value>
        <settlementGenerationWeight>0</settlementGenerationWeight>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- And it cannot appear spontaneously later in the run. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OuterRim_RebelAlliance"]/canMakeRandomly</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OuterRim_RebelAlliance"]/canMakeRandomly</xpath>
      <value>
        <canMakeRandomly>false</canMakeRandomly>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- Off the world-creation picker, so it cannot be re-added by accident. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OuterRim_RebelAlliance"]/maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OuterRim_RebelAlliance"]/maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation</xpath>
      <value>
        <maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>0</maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
